  "policy_prompt_for_action": [
    {
      "modify_from": "At cube_lifted, always command a separate closed-gripper alignment at the target center and nominal z=0.15 m before lowering, including repeated placements already nearly centered over the target. Construct the center-corrected hover waypoint first. If its positional displacement from the current TCP is less than 2 mm, retain the target-center x,y and raise the waypoint z by 3–5 mm to satisfy the minimum displacement. Only after observing completion of this alignment recognize target_hover and apply descent-and-release. Allow ordinary small tracking errors and very short nonzero alignment motions when recognizing completion; do not skip alignment or recognize it merely because it was commanded.",
      "modify_to": "At cube_lifted, independently localize the target center and compare it with the current TCP position. If the lateral distance to that center is at most approximately 1.5 mm and the TCP height is within 2 mm of z=0.15 m, descend directly at the localized target-center x,y to commanded z=0.005 m and open. Make this decision before applying the minimum-displacement safeguard; do not manufacture an upward hover when direct descent applies. Otherwise command a separate closed-gripper alignment at the target center and nominal z=0.15 m. Construct this center-corrected hover waypoint first; if its positional displacement from the current TCP is less than 2 mm, retain the target-center x,y and add a 3–5 mm upward displacement sufficient to satisfy the minimum. After observing completion of this separate alignment, recognize target_hover and apply its descent-and-release rule. Allow ordinary small tracking errors and very short nonzero alignment motions when recognizing completion, but do not use that broader completion tolerance to decide whether alignment can be omitted. Never recognize target_hover merely because alignment was commanded, or because direct descent was selected. Following direct descent, retain cube_lifted until release is observed, then apply the existing release milestone and placement-count rules."
    }
  ],
  "refused": "No substantive change requested this round is refused. This replaces Round 2's unconditional separate-alignment requirement because the current report identifies it as the cause of unnecessary hover actions. It does not restore the earlier blanket omission for every hover waypoint within 2 mm: direct descent instead requires both the tighter lateral alignment condition and the nominal-height condition. Necessary small corrective alignments retain the minimum-displacement safeguard and observed-completion requirement. Localization, memory fields, release counting, and final withdrawal remain unchanged."
}
